[00:00.00]Amazing grace! How sweet the sound
[00:04.00]That saved a wretch like me!
[00:08.00]I once was lost, but now am found,
[00:12.00]Was blind, but now I see.
[00:16.00]'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear,
[00:20.00]And grace my fears relieved;
[00:24.00]How precious did that grace appear
[00:28.00]The hour I first believed!
[00:32.00]When we've been there ten thousand years,
[00:36.00]Bright shining as the sun,
[00:40.00]We've no less days to sing God's praise
[00:44.00]Than when we'd first begun.